From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:28:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] B70-V32-HC1: hot/cold on 0.32: B70_MOE_COLD_EXPERTS=N
 (cold per layer per rank), stock -1 remap as a helper, CPU tests

- B70_MOE_COLD_EXPERTS=N names the cold count per layer per rank and wins over B70_MOE_HOT_EXPERTS, so one
  number means the same VRAM saving at TP4 (N of 128) and TP2 (N of 256). B70_MOE_HOTCOLD=1 without either
  count keeps everything resident (no plan): the 4-card all-resident layout is unchanged unless a def names N.
- remap_unrouted(): the 0.32 stock remap of topk_ids == -1, shared by the hot/cold call.
- tests/model_executor/test_b70_hotcold_v032.py: off unless switched; no count = all resident; EP4 (8, 16 cold)
  and EP2 (138 cold) plans per rank; COLD wins over HOT; clamping; rankings at EP4; remap_unrouted; the learned
  state is read per engine prefix (two engines on one host never mix their files).
